//RS //! D-CLIFLAG1 (c7cliflag): typed entry-signature CLI parsing.
//RS //!
//RS //! `#[CLI]` is a sibling derive of `#[Codable]` on the same marker/derive
//RS //! infrastructure (D-VERDICT-732-1, formerly D-MARKERMOVE1; D-CLIFLAG1).
//RS //! A `#[CLI]`-derived struct's
//RS //! fields each map to one `core.args` registration; see Docs/spec/spec.md
//RS //! ("Typed entry-signature CLI parsing (D-CLIFLAG1)") for the pinned
//RS //! field-mapping rule this validates. Sema does the shape-checking here so
//RS //! `Codegen/Items.rs::emit_struct_cli` can emit unconditionally (I3: sema
//RS //! decides, codegen never re-derives "is this field supported").
//RS //!
//RS //! D-CLI-POS1=A: required value fields also fill from bare argv in declaration
//RS //! order unless `#[Flag]` opts them out. Bool / optional / defaulted stay
//RS //! flag-only; every field still accepts `--field`, and named input wins.
//RS //!
//RS //! Also validates program-struct callable members and the `fn run` entry-
//RS //! parameter shape (E1308, invoked from the entry-point check beside the
//RS //! existing `run` checks).
